From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0037] meson-vdec: VP9/HEVC ISR must not start a picture once teardown began

vdec_stop_streaming() sets sess->stopping before vdec_poweroff() drains the codec.
A picture interrupt that the threaded ISR handles after drain() has returned the
DPB (flush_output) and reset the reference map started a new picture anyway: it
took a CAPTURE buffer that nothing returned any more (vb2 WARN in
__vb2_queue_cancel: "stop_streaming operation is leaving buffer N in active
state") and decoded an inter frame with no references ("codec_vp9_sync_ref:
couldn't find VP9 ref -1", seen on #90 with a slowed client). The threaded ISR
now leaves the picture alone when stopping is set. flush_output()/stop() take
the same codec lock, so the ISR either finishes before the flush (and its buffer
is returned by it) or sees stopping. stopping is only cleared when streaming
resumes, and a STREAMOFF of either queue in RUNNING always runs the full teardown,
so the flag cannot stay set on a running session.

Validated on #98: 20 VP9 seeks at full speed and 15 with the client slowed to
~14 fps (capture hook computing a CRC of every destination frame): no 'ref -1',
no 'active state', no WARN; 10 VP9<->HEVC session switches with a seek in each.

---
diff -ruN s95/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c s37/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -1491,6 +1491,17 @@
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	mutex_lock(&hevc->lock);
+	/*
+	 * h96 0037 (24.09.2026): teardown already started. vdec_poweroff() has
+	 * (or is about to have) flushed the frame list and reset the reference
+	 * map; starting this picture now takes a CAPTURE buffer that nothing
+	 * returns (vb2: "leaving buffer N in active state") and decodes an
+	 * inter frame with no references ("couldn't find VP9 ref -1").
+	 * stopping is set first thing in vdec_stop_streaming() and only cleared
+	 * when streaming resumes; the codec lock orders it against drain().
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(sess->stopping))
+		goto unlock;
 	if (dec_status != HEVC_SLICE_SEGMENT_DONE) {
 		dev_err(core->dev_dec, "Unrecognized dec_status: %08X\n",
 			dec_status);
diff -ruN s95/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c s37/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
@@ -2554,6 +2554,17 @@
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	mutex_lock(&vp9->lock);
+	/*
+	 * h96 0037 (24.09.2026): teardown already started. vdec_poweroff() has
+	 * (or is about to have) flushed the frame list and reset the reference
+	 * map; starting this picture now takes a CAPTURE buffer that nothing
+	 * returns (vb2: "leaving buffer N in active state") and decodes an
+	 * inter frame with no references ("couldn't find VP9 ref -1").
+	 * stopping is set first thing in vdec_stop_streaming() and only cleared
+	 * when streaming resumes; the codec lock orders it against drain().
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(sess->stopping))
+		goto unlock;
 	if (dec_status != VP9_HEAD_PARSER_DONE) {
 		dev_err(core->dev_dec, "Unrecognized dec_status: %08X\n",
 			dec_status);
